<!--
  BASELINE FIXTURE - do not edit to match the shipped catalogue.

  The four heart palettes and five heart maps exactly as they stood on dev at 4f66331, the
  commit before the camp landed. A settlement founded before that build decodes to THESE
  definitions, so a test that wants to prove what a pre-change save does at its next
  improvement must compile these, not the current maps with a placement deleted. Overlaid onto
  the live corpus by KingdomArchitectureCorpusFixture.Overlay, together with the civic-heart
  plan: its tier requirements belong to the old build as much as its rows do, and a map that
  predates a required anchor cannot be compiled against the tier that demands it. Every other
  palette, map, plan, pose and catalogue row stays current, which is exactly the mixed world an
  old save loads into.

  The root tag is deliberately NOT <KingdomArchitectures>: every tool that enumerates authored
  architecture walks the whole checkout for that tag (Tools/gallery_cases.py:77-86), and a
  fixture that answered to it would be counted as a ninth shipped stream and double every heart
  case in the gallery census. This file is read by exactly one caller, by path.

  If the heart maps are ever REPLACED again, this file stays as it is: it records a shipped
  past, not an intention.
-->
